#====================================================================
# Draft: Samba waf testonly on OHOS - shell + TAP + tdbtorture
#        execution taxonomy and the --disable-python guard that stops
#        python binding tests from false-failing (tdb 1.4.15)
#====================================================================

id:                     DRAFT-11055-WAF-TESTONLY-EXECUTION-ACCOUNTING
trigger_tool:           waf|make|python|test
phase:                  testing
error_signature:        Python test failed: PYTHONPATH=bin/python|python testsuite returned 1|ModuleNotFoundError.*tdb|ImportError.*tdb

severity:               2
category:               testing, waf, ohos, python
match_keywords:         testonly, make test, tdb1_unit_tests, TAP, RUN_PYTHON_TESTS, python_interpreters, disable-python, tdbtorture, test-output, test accounting, upstream test pass rate

title:                  Samba waf testonly on OHOS: shell integration + TAP binaries + tdbtorture through one entry point, and the env.disable_python guard required because --disable-python still runs python binding tests

root_cause:             The wscript testonly task in Samba-family standalone packages is a fixed pipeline: shell integration scripts -> per-test TAP binaries -> tdbtorture stress -> RUN_PYTHON_TESTS. It does not consult --disable-python: SAMBA_CHECK_PYTHON still records python3 in env.python_interpreters even when python bindings are disabled, so make test runs python/tests/simple.py against a package that has no pytdb module, fails with ImportError and turns the whole upstream test run red. Per-test output is redirected to a single test-output file and only cat'ed on failure, so per-test accounting must be reconstructed from the "..." progress lines plus the wscript test list.

affected_scope:         Upstream test execution and truthful pass-rate accounting for all Samba wafsamba standalone packages (tdb/talloc/ldb/tevent and same-family projects) on OHOS, especially C-only packages built with --disable-python. Verified instance: tdb 1.4.15 (37 TAP tests + 2 shell tests + tdbtorture).

verification_cmd:       make test   # expect: "...tdb1-*" x len(wscript tdb1_unit_tests), "testsuite returned 0", "python testsuite skipped (--disable-python)"

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           guard-testonly-python-tests-and-count-from-wscript-list
rec_description:        When building a C-only package with --disable-python, guard the testonly python step with env.disable_python and print an explicit skip line instead of running it (patch the wscript, do not touch upstream test cases). Account the pass rate from the authoritative source: count the "..." progress lines and reconcile them with the wscript tdb1_unit_tests list length (37 for tdb 1.4.15), count shell "success:" lines, and take the tdbtorture return code; report the python binding tests separately as "not enabled (optional binding)" rather than "passed" or "upstream has none".
rec_command:            make test 2>&1 | grep -c '^\.\.\.tdb1-'   # = 37; grep 'testsuite returned'; grep 'python testsuite skipped'
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               archives/t/tdb/1.4.15/patches/0002-wscript.patch (env.disable_python guard in testonly)

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      run-suite-from-testonly-scripts-directly
fallback_description:   If the guarded wscript cannot be used (e.g. testing an unpatched tree), run the two shell tests and the tdb1-* binaries manually from bin/st/tdb-tests with TEST_DATA_PREFIX set and record per-test exit codes; keep the same accounting rules.
fallback_command:       see tdb 1.4.15 notes.md "编译步骤" for the manual sequence
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:

forbid_1_pattern:       comment out RUN_PYTHON_TESTS|delete python/tests/simple.py|mask the python test failure|stub import tdb|report binding tests as passed
forbid_1_reason:        Deleting or masking upstream test calls is R9 (fake pass) territory; a stub tdb module would fake the pass rate; binding tests that were not run must be reported as not-enabled, with the technical reason.
forbid_1_consequence:   Deceptive-adaptation finding in W4/preflight review; invalidates the upstream pass-rate claim of the PR.

principles:             real-evidence-over-assumption, minimal-patch, honest-test-accounting
